  m_text: 'found in areas with quartz veins, mineralized fault lines, and ancient
    riverbeds. Prospectors study maps, soil types, and rock formations to determine
    which locations are likely to contain deposits. Many gold-bearing regions are
    tied to past volcanic activity or shifting tectonic plates. By learning how gold
    forms and moves through erosion, prospectors can focus their efforts more effectively.


    Safety
    is an important consideration for anyone engaged in gold prospecting. Remote
    environments may present hazards such as unstable ground, wildlife encounters,
    and unpredictable weather. Prospectors should always carry proper gear, including
    first aid supplies, navigation tools, and communication devices. Checking local
    regulations and obtaining necessary permits helps ensure a legal and safe experience.
    Responsible prospecting involves respecting both nature and established rules.'
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
