  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: 'Another type of gold frequently found is flake or dust gold, which consists
    of tiny, thin pieces or particles dispersed throughout sediment.


    A third
    type is gold embedded in quartz veins, often called lode or hard rock gold. Unlike
    nuggets and flakes found in loose sediment, this gold is trapped within solid
    rock formations and requires extraction through mining or crushing.'
